  "metadata": {
    "job": "Clamped toolplate",
    "revision": "A",
    "notes": "The clamps are a generator feature on a fixture layer, so pre-flight treats them as keep-outs — drag one over the pocket and machined-fixture reports an error. The pocket is roughed adaptive because 14mm deep with a ⌀6 cutter is where contour-parallel loading spikes. The plate is never cut free: it stays clamped."
  },
